{"parentUuid":"9282f70d-903f-47e8-9ae1-ffd9cc65cd6a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RFbwTwpj9pGmQYM81L4kk9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Root cause\n\nMigration is repacking checkpoints whose **archived `/full/<n>` generations were created before April 13, 2026**, when raw transcripts were renamed from `full.jsonl` → `raw_transcript` (commit `a3cd77122`).\n\nThe chain:\n\n1. `migrateOneCheckpoint` calls the fast path (`v2CheckpointFullyMigrated`) and the slow path (`collectMissingFullSessionsForPacking`). Both rely on `V2GitStore.HasFullSessionArtifacts` → `inspectFullSessionArtifacts` (`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go:152`).\n2. That function only recognizes the new names — it sets `HasTranscript`/`HasHash` only when it sees `raw_transcript`, `raw_transcript.NNN`, or `raw_transcript_hash.txt`. Legacy `full.jsonl`/`content_hash.txt` files are ignored.\n3. So for a checkpoint whose artifacts live in a pre-rename archived generation, `hasFullSessionArtifacts` returns false on every rerun.\n4. The slow path then treats the session as \"missing\", appends it to `fullCheckpoint`, and the `generationPacker` writes a brand-new archived generation with the new naming. Old archives are **not** cleaned up: `CleanupV1TranscriptFiles` (`v2_committed.go:869`) explicitly only touches `/full/current`, not archives.\n5. Result: 46 legacy archives + 40 freshly-packed new-format archives = 86, and another rerun would just keep growing because the legacy ones are still unreadable to the check.\n\nThe fast-path commit `7d09b51a4` from today doesn't help here — it short-circuits the *same* check and returns `errAlreadyMigrated` only when the artifacts are recognized, which they aren't for the legacy layout.\n\nTests cover the post-rename rerun case (`REDACTED`) but nothing covers archived generations written under the old name.\n\n## Suggested fix (want to confirm before coding)\n\nTwo-part change:\n\n1. **`inspectFullSessionArtifacts`** — also accept `paths.TranscriptFileName` / `TranscriptFileName.NNN` / `paths.ContentHashFileName` as valid full-session artifacts. This stops the duplication on every future rerun.\n2. **`readTranscriptFromObjectTree`** (`v2_read.go:443`) — fall back to the same legacy names, so the existing legacy archives are actually readable by current code (`ReadSessionContent` etc.). Without this, the 46 old archives in your repo stay unreadable even though we'd now claim they're \"fully migrated.\"\n\nAdd a regression test: legacy-named files in an archived `/full/<n>` ref → rerun is a no-op (no new generation, `skipped=1`).\n\nOpen question for you: do you also want a one-shot rename pass that rewrites legacy archives to the new names (and/or prunes the now-duplicated legacy archives in your repo)? That's a bigger change with rewriting commits on `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/*`, so I'd rather get a steer before doing it.\n\nWant me to go ahead with parts (1) + (2) + the regression test?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2186,"cache_read_input_tokens":138742,"output_tokens":1280,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2186,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1280,"cache_read_input_tokens":138742,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2186},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cai4ZqN1fjc6ctBbwPFf6","attributionSkill":"superpowers:systematic-debugging","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"971b32ed-0c49-4cac-a4e4-47f15b3da788","timestamp":"2026-05-04T19:14:36.912Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli","s