{"parentUuid":"83a18e23-892d-4cad-ab86-08b4177bab3c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GYA9gkLGtUAUZzJr1vAw8f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The repair/backfill machinery wasn't dropped in by accident — it was added deliberately, but in many small steps where each step had a narrow justification. Here's the chronology:\n\n**PR #891 (2026-04-03 → 2026-04-09) \"Checkpoints V2: add migration option\"** — by computermode\n\n- Initial commit `7d099f9a` (Apr 3) added `migrate.go` with `backfillCompactTranscripts` already included. Compact-transcript backfill on rerun was baked in from day one of the migrate command.\n- Follow-up commit `119e24ffea` (Apr 7) \"Check for any missing components when rerunning a backfill\" added `repairPartialV2Checkpoint` and `hasCurrentFullSessionArtifacts`. This is the commit that introduced the broader \"if rerun finds a half-migrated checkpoint, finish it instead of skipping\" behavior.\n\n  **Stated intent**: a prior migration that crashed mid-batch leaves checkpoints with /main written but /full not packed; the user shouldn't have to know about that and shouldn't have to use `--force` — rerun should just pick up where it left off.\n\n**PR #1034 (Apr 24) \"fix/duplicate-full-transcript\"** — Sven Pfleiderer\n\n- Commit `0173541c93` \"Clean up v1-named transcript files on /full/current during update\" added `CleanupV1TranscriptFiles` to **`updateCommittedFullTranscript`** (the runtime stop-time path). Reason: when an agent committed against a checkpoint that already had legacy `full.jsonl` files (from a pre-rename CLI), the runtime write was leaving both `full.jsonl` *and* the new `raw_transcript` side-by-side — duplicates.\n- Commit `d19e13c4a` \"Move v1 transcript cleanup from updateCommittedFullTranscript to migrate\" then yanked it out of the hot path: legacy-file cleanup is migration-specific and shouldn't run on every stop-time finalization. Hooked it into the rerun-repair flow.\n\n**PR #1080 (Apr 30) \"Checkpoints v2: Fix issue where migrations didn't check archived v2 transcripts\"** — was actually fixing a previous version of the bug *you* just hit:\n\n- Before this PR, the repair check only looked at `/full/current`. A previous migration that had rotated artifacts into `/full/<n>` would, on rerun, look \"missing\" — and the repair would re-pack them, **also** rehydrating /full/current. Subsequent ordinary writes then crossed the rotation threshold and produced more archived gens.\n- Fix: generalized `hasCurrentFullSessionArtifacts` → `hasFullSessionArtifacts` to walk current + archived. Same shape of bug as today's, different trigger.\n\n**PR a0b641121 (Apr 30) \"Repair migrated v2 generation metadata\"** — Sven\n\n- Renamed `repairPartialV2Checkpoint` → `collectMissingFullCheckpointForPacking` and rewired the repair so missing /full sessions go through the same `generationPacker` as fresh migrations, instead of being written straight to /full/current. Cleaner rotation semantics.\n\n**Commit 7d09b51a4 (today) \"Add fast path checks for checkpoints migrations\"** — computermode\n\n- Added `v2CheckpointFullyMigrated` predicate + the `agent==\"\"` skip inside backfill. Same author who put the original repair logic in. This was a perf bandage *over* the now-large slow path: short-circuit when everything looks clean, but leave the slow path intact.\n\n**The pattern.** The original goal in PR #891 — \"be forgiving on rerun if a previous migration was interrupted\" — is reasonable. But the implementation chosen (\"inspect existing v2 state and silently fix what's missing\") had a fundamental design problem: the consistency check has to know about every way v2 state could be partially-out-of-the-current format. Each of those PRs is fixing or extending that check:\n\n- archived vs current generation locations (#1080)\n- runtime path leaving legacy names alongside new ones (#1034 first half)\n- legacy names on first migration (#1034 second half — moved into repair)\n- compact transcripts left empty by older migration runs (initial backfill)\n\nToday's bug is the same family: archived gens written under legacy `full.jsonl` aren't recognized as \"have full artifacts\" so the repair fires and packs duplicates.\n\nYour \"skip, full stop\" rule eliminates the whole class. The legitimate use case (interrupted migration recovery) is *still* available via `--force`, which already prunes-and-redoes the affected checkpoints. If a finer-grained \"resume the interrupted run without redoing complete checkpoints\" mode is ever wanted again, it deserves to be its own explicit flag, not the silent default behavior of the no-flag invocation."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1162,"cache_read_input_tokens":305815,"output_tokens":3439,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1162,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3439,"cache_read_input_tokens":305815,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1162},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaiF58AGrK6G8g6tjB6Pt","type":"assistant","uuid":"0b7dd435-9ea7-424b-a585-f1e575816080","timestamp":"2026-05-04T21:32:57.163Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"c4966049-2d73-4daf-9e0c-914f4a7685de","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"more-migration-speedups"}
